      "limitations": "Same refined silver material per signed kg, using the complete native regional storage supply mix instead of only its lead-derived supplier. Native supply includes lead, copper, combined gold-silver and secondary-scrap routes plus its internal freight. Preserve the existing four-route mix once; do not reconstruct source market shares, apply the native shares a second time, create a zero-burden silver stock or add extra refining/recovery credits. Treatment-named source providers supply allocated positive-reference silver products here, not waste services, so no waste sign flip is applied. Source global market and native historical2006 European supply have different route shares, coproduct allocation, recovery, geography, delivery and vintage. Source product information reports99.5% silver while native route documentation includes99.9%; preserve the declared product kg with no invented purity multiplier and no specific assay/grade or LCIA-equivalence claim. The native parent description partly refers to lead processing, but its actual complete supply vector establishes all four routes. Native biosphere exclusions and unquantified score differences remain explicit. Only the inspected ecoinvent3.12 cut-off market is admitted."
